# NOITE's street escape (3fstreet) starts the real XILINDRO, which loses:
# no key (xilindro-alone-lose.input). NOITE shows itself, adds -1000 and
# goes to the 3fstree1 cutscene, which takes a life (2 left) and goes back
# to the prison (3fprisao).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fstreet --ms 80000 --input tools/play/xilindro-3fstreet-lose.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fstreet --ms 140000 --fix all --input tools/play/xilindro-3fstreet-lose.input
#
# XILINDRO starts at 26295 (xilindro-3fstreet-win.input); its window
# closes at 64645 (Original) or near 128 s (`--fix all`: the easy opponent,
# below).
# The Corrigida (`--fix all`) shows XILINDRO's controls screen first; Enter takes
# it down 50 ms after it opened, PORRADA stands for 2 s (the frozen intro,
# `fight_controls.start_delay_ms`) and the round then plays as the
# Original's from its start, 2050 ms later (`delay`: every later line
# moves too).
26345 ?fight_controls_screen key return
26345 ?fight_controls_screen delay 2050
40000 dump fight
# The Corrigida's fight (`fight_fair`, `fight_easy_ai`) takes longer: the 90-s clock ends it, XILINDRO closes near 128 s.
+0 ?fight_fair wait 3fstree1 90000
+0 wait 3fstree1 40000
+0 result lost -1000
+0 wait 3fprisao 10000
+0 state
